          "text": "Dear Patient,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. Seizures began at age 77. The epilepsy is structural in etiology, with MRI demonstrating hippocampal sclerosis. Current seizure frequency is approximately 3 per year.\n\n**Current Medications:**  \n- Zonisamide  \n- Levetiracetam  \n\n**Seizure Burden Summary:**  \nFocal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures, approximately 3 per year. Epilepsy is drug-responsive.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures, with structural etiology and MRI evidence of hippocampal sclerosis.\n\n**Plan:**  \nContinue current antiseizure medications, zonisamide and levetiracetam. Continue clinical monitoring of seizure frequency and follow up in epilepsy clinic.",
